                            <comment id="15364608" author="dmagda" created="Wed, 6 Jul 2016 16:48:17 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?name=samaitra&quot; class=&quot;user-hover&quot; rel=&quot;samaitra&quot;&gt;samaitra&lt;/a&gt;, please use the approach suggested by Yakov above. In your current implementation the whole operation is not atomic. Use &lt;tt&gt;cache.invoke&lt;/tt&gt; - it was suggested by Yakov when he mentioned &lt;tt&gt;EntryProcessor&lt;/tt&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="15366663" author="samaitra" created="Thu, 7 Jul 2016 19:45:32 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?name=dmagda&quot; class=&quot;user-hover&quot; rel=&quot;dmagda&quot;&gt;dmagda&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Hi Denis,&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Thank you for reviewing the PR. I have changed the implementation to use EntryProcessor. There are two cases, one when cacheAtomicityMode is TRANSACTIONAL and when it is not. In case of Transactional cache I have used IgniteInternalTx otherwise the unit tests fails because the transaction is automatically rollbacked. In case of non transactional cache we get error transactional mode is not supported in non-transactional cache.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Please review the changes and let me know if any further change is required.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Regards&lt;br/&gt;
Saikat&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="15370451" author="dmagda" created="Mon, 11 Jul 2016 09:34:55 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;Hi Saikat, thanks I&apos;ll take a look at your changes tomorrow.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="15371029" author="samaitra" created="Mon, 11 Jul 2016 15:54:24 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?name=dmagda&quot; class=&quot;user-hover&quot; rel=&quot;dmagda&quot;&gt;dmagda&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

